From fc538bde07a7fe6bd548ac0214e4d3ef5b992c9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:11:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] batch: STRATA_READ_YIELD is off beside
 STRATA_PIPED_MTP, STRATA_KVA, the elastic K/V and without the prompt cache,
 so every read path takes a BYIELD as without it (#656's give_way) instead of
 answering YIELDNO final (STRATA_READ_YIELD, fixup of 044326f8)

yield_arm refused every BYIELD there with YIELDNO final, while the
request paths had already swallowed the line (the concurrent loop's
continue, the pieces' ys = -1): #656's preemption was gone altogether,
worse than the switch being unset, and the server, without INFO
read_yield, still sent BYIELD by the #656 rule. One read_yield_on,
decided before READY, now stands for read_yield_env() on every request
path; the boot line names the reason. Production (a 4-card split, the
prompt cache, none of the three) is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
